align-empty-encrypted-parameter: reject an empty encrypted parameter that ends the command

Classification: profile setting (implementation-defined behavior, not a spec deviation).

An encrypted first parameter that is an empty TPM2B ending the command is
rejected with TPM_RC_SIZE, as tpm-rs and the TCG reference's
CryptParameterDecryption() (`bufferSize <= 0`) do. The specification defines
no error for this case; the upstream IBM code executes the command, which
would leave the session (nonceTPM) and the TPM state of the TPMs different,
so it cannot be a harness exception.

diff --git a/src/CryptUtil.c b/src/CryptUtil.c
--- a/src/CryptUtil.c
+++ b/src/CryptUtil.c
@@ -1018,7 +1018,15 @@ CryptParameterDecryption(
 	    return TPM_RC_INSUFFICIENT;
 	}
 
-    if(cipherSize > bufferSize)
+    // tpm-rs differential testing (implementation-defined behavior aligned
+    // with tpm-rs and mstpm20, NOT a spec deviation): an encrypted parameter
+    // that is an empty TPM2B ending the command is rejected with TPM_RC_SIZE,
+    // as the TCG reference's CryptParameterDecryption() (`bufferSize <= 0`)
+    // does. The specification defines no error for this case; the upstream
+    // IBM code executes the command, which would leave the session (nonceTPM)
+    // and TPM state of the two TPMs different, so it cannot be a harness
+    // exception.
+    if(cipherSize > bufferSize || bufferSize <= 0)
 	{
 	    return TPM_RC_SIZE;
 	}
